                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/905: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-27T10:00:00+08:00">October 27, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>933. Department’s 355, October 17, 9 p.m. I see no objection to your informing
                    Davis of my conversation with Moss. I am urging Foreign Office to reply to the
                    Legation’s note of October 31, 1929.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
